  "response_text": "The stack allocation method can be described starting with the max stack size (denoted by the constant variable MAX_STACK_SIZE), which for the lab was set to 0x4000 bytes. Inside this limited stack space, there is one main stack size which is already defined in the operating system code, and as many desired thread stacks that can fit in the max stack size which is, also defined by the user. Assuming we have the value for MSP_INIT_VAL, the PSP value can simply be determined by subtracting the size of the main stack. It\u2019s important to note that when computing to use the integer value of the MSP_INIT_VAL. It\u2019s important to know the initial location of MSP so that the PSP can be properly inserted into the downward stack.\\n",
